{
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "name": "Sport",
  "theme": "sportdash",
  "_about": "After BMW's Live Cockpit Sport view (photos of the X3's own cluster, measured on a warped overlay), generated by design/gen_sport.py (edit that and regenerate): blue speed (0..200 mph) and red rev (0..7000 rpm, the M40i's own scale) brackets, each a bright outer line, a filling band, a dark gap and an inner line. The middle is black; 'Leave room for the map' cuts it see-through for BMW's map, inset 'holeInset' px with 'holeRadius' corners. Everything that isn't text is one shader (sdash). The brackets and the gear keep clear of the black box BMW draws at x 1406..1597, y 342..419, and of the hood over the top corners. Widget reference: shared/hud.js header. Under the right rpm scale (y 640, beside the red strip's end) the car ahead (\"--\" with no car ahead): its gap ({{accGap}} m / ft) and its speed against ours ({{accRel}}, minus = closing). The map window keeps a triangle in each corner black (holeCut), where BMW's own Sport view draws bracket ends, a gauge icon and hatched dial ends (car photo, Nov 7 2026). The bottom strip is two bars from its middle out: the throttle to the left (its last tenth red in kickdown), the brake to the right (while the brake lights are on, how hard the car slows, on a log scale). Under the left speed scale, boost (BST, 0..1.5 bar, yellow) over the 12 V battery (BAT, its charge %, green), below the bracket's bottom line, each with its value at the end (the battery's in V). The bottom row: the clock at the left with the range beside it, coolant and outside temperature at the right; its middle is kept free (for a music title later). The map window also keeps a strip along its left edge black (holeMask, x 418..482 y 408..445: just above the fuel gauge, below BMW's speed so its hundreds digit shows), where BMW's speed-limit sign pokes out (car photo, Nov 8 2026).",
